# trivy allowlist — CVEs accepted for the images CI scans.
#
# Consumed by ci.yml's `trivy` job (severity CRITICAL, --ignore-unfixed), which
# scans deploy/images/claude-code/Dockerfile's built image. One CVE id per line;
# `#` starts a comment. Trivy applies this file verbatim — an id here is
# silenced everywhere, so keep the scope note in the comment.
#
# RULES for adding an entry (this file is a security exception log, not a mute
# button): every id needs a comment naming (1) the package, (2) WHY it does not
# reach us in this image, and (3) the date + who accepted it. An entry with no
# reason is a finding someone hid. Delete an entry the moment the base image
# ships a fix — --ignore-unfixed already suppresses the no-fix-available case,
# so anything listed here is a CVE we could have patched and chose not to.
#
# Empty on purpose: the current agent image has no accepted CRITICALs.
